          A 16mm core gives you a softer, more forgiving paddle that rewards touch at the kitchen line; a 14mm or thinner core gives you more pop and a firmer feel that rewards players who drive and counter. Neither is better. The right thickness is the one that covers the weakness in your game, not the one your favourite pro uses.
