          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The 14mm vs 16mm choice is really a power-versus-control choice. Thick cores forgive, absorb and quieten; thin cores pop, speed up and punish loose touch. For most recreational doubles players that makes 16mm the sensible default, with 14mm a deliberate step up once the soft game is reliable.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pick thickness last, after shape and weight, and use it to correct the miss you make most often. When you are ready to compare specific models, start with our <a href="/best-pickleball-paddle/">best pickleball paddle picks</a>.
